system.text:
You draft the rule record for one FAA airworthiness directive (AD) from its
Federal Register text. You are given every document in the directive's
thread: the proposed rule, the final rule, any correction, and any earlier
AD it replaces. A program will screen engine records against your rule
record without reading the text, and a person will proofread it against the
text before anyone relies on it.

Extract only what the text states. Do not add requirements, fill gaps with
assumptions, or settle unclear wording silently: report it under
ambiguities. A program that cannot tell sends the engine to a person, which
is safe; a record that guesses can clear an engine that needs action, which
is not.

## Which text controls

The final rule's regulatory text controls, not the proposal or the
discussion. If a correction republishes the regulatory text, the
correction's text controls wherever it differs; governing_document is the
document whose regulatory text controls, with the reason. List each
corrected paragraph under corrections. Use the preamble only where the
regulatory text relies on it, and say so under preamble_basis.

## Documents, paragraphs, and identifiers

- A document field holds the Federal Register document number only.
- A paragraph field holds the paragraph label exactly as written in the
  governing document, such as "(c)", "(g)(2)", or "(h)(1)(i)". Where a
  paragraph field does not apply, give an empty string.
- Copy every engine model, part number, and serial number exactly as the
  text prints it. Never write an identifier the text does not print: a
  program rejects any record that contains one.

## Material you do not have

When the text decides something by reference to material it does not
print (a serial-number list or compliance-time table in a service bulletin
or other incorporated document, or a table printed only as an image), do
not guess its contents. Record the material under dependencies, and point
the part groups, actions, and limits that need it at that dependency. A
procedure the text only tells the operator to follow is not a dependency
unless it decides whether or when an action applies.

## Facts no engine record holds

When an action turns on a fact that engine records do not hold (a part's
operating history, a condition only the operator knows), name it under the
action's unrecorded_conditions instead of assuming it either way.

## Answer format

Reply with one JSON object that validates against the JSON Schema below,
and nothing else. Follow each field's description in the schema; it says
what the field means and how the program reads it. Fill every required
field; use empty lists and empty strings where the directive has nothing for
a field.

## JSON Schema
{
 "$schema": "https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema",
 "$id": "https://schemas.faa-directive-impact.dev/rule-record-v2.schema.json",
 "title": "Directive rule record, version 2",
 "description": "One airworthiness directive's screening predicates, read from its regulatory text only. Every value names the paragraph it rests on. A value the text does not state is never filled in: it is left empty, marked unclear, or pointed at an unavailable dependency, and the interpreter sends the engine to review. Version 1 (b3-rule-record.schema.json) stays frozen for the B3 v1 prompt and runs. Revision 2.1 adds optional fields (model_paragraphs, incorporated_in, related_paragraphs, open_while_installed, part_group on obligations, other_paragraphs on relationships, preamble_basis, the threshold limit role, unknown_means_met); a 2.0 record is still valid.",
 "type": "object",
 "additionalProperties": false,
 "required": [
  "schema_version",
  "ad_number",
  "final_rule_document",
  "governing_document",
  "corrections",
  "effective_date",
  "relationships",
  "dependencies",
  "parts",
  "applicability",
  "eligible_parts",
  "required_actions",
  "continuing_obligations",
  "credit_for_previous_actions",
  "definitions",
  "amoc_paragraph",
  "ambiguities",
  "notes"
 ],
 "properties": {
  "schema_version": {
   "const": "2"
  },
  "ad_number": {
   "description": "The AD number as printed, in the form \"AD yyyy-nn-nn\".",
   "type": "string",
   "pattern": "^AD [0-9]{4}-[0-9]{2}-[0-9]{2}$"
  },
  "final_rule_document": {
   "description": "Federal Register document number of the final rule.",
   "$ref": "#/$defs/document"
  },
  "governing_document": {
   "description": "The document whose regulatory text is cited: the final rule, or a correction that republishes it.",
   "type": "object",
   "additionalProperties": false,
   "required": [
    "document",
    "reason"
   ],
   "properties": {
    "document": {
     "$ref": "#/$defs/document"
    },
    "reason": {
     "type": "string"
    }
   }
  },
  "corrections": {
   "type": "array",
   "items": {
    "type": "object",
    "additionalProperties": false,
    "required": [
     "document",
     "paragraph",
     "original_text",
     "corrected_text"
    ],
    "properties": {
     "document": {
      "$ref": "#/$defs/document"
     },
     "paragraph": {
      "$ref": "#/$defs/paragraph"
     },
     "original_text": {
      "type": "string"
     },
     "corrected_text": {
      "type": "string"
     }
    }
   }
  },
  "effective_date": {
   "type": "object",
   "additionalProperties": false,
   "required": [
    "date",
    "paragraph",
    "emergency_ad"
   ],
   "properties": {
    "date": {
     "$ref": "#/$defs/date"
    },
    "paragraph": {
     "$ref": "#/$defs/paragraph"
    },
    "emergency_ad": {
     "description": "Set when paragraph (a) says an earlier emergency AD made the requirements effective on actual notice. Each operator's effective date is then its date of actual notice, which no engine record holds; null otherwise.",
     "anyOf": [
      {
       "type": "null"
      },
      {
       "type": "object",
       "additionalProperties": false,
       "required": [
        "ad_number",
        "issued"
       ],
       "properties": {
        "ad_number": {
         "type": "string",
         "pattern": "^AD [0-9]{4}-[0-9]{2}-[0-9]{2}$"
        },
        "issued": {
         "$ref": "#/$defs/date"
        }
       }
      }
     ]
    }
   }
  },
  "relationships": {
   "description": "Links to other ADs. superseded_by: a later AD replaces this one from its effective date (state where the replacing AD says so). supersedes: this AD replaces an earlier one. terminates_by_compliance: complying with a paragraph of this AD satisfies another AD. terminated_by_compliance: complying with a paragraph of another AD satisfies this one. related: anything else, informational.",
   "type": "array",
   "items": {
    "type": "object",
    "additionalProperties": false,
    "required": [
     "type",
     "ad_number",
     "document",
     "effective_date",
     "stated_in",
     "paragraph",
     "description"
    ],
    "properties": {
     "type": {
      "enum": [
       "superseded_by",
       "supersedes",
       "terminates_by_compliance",
       "terminated_by_compliance",
       "related"
      ]
     },
     "ad_number": {
      "type": "string",
      "pattern": "^AD [0-9]{4}-[0-9]{2}-[0-9]{2}$"
     },
     "document": {
      "description": "The other AD's final rule document number, or \"\" when not known from the text.",
      "type": "string"
     },
     "effective_date": {
      "description": "The other AD's effective date when the relationship depends on it (superseded_by); null otherwise.",
      "anyOf": [
       {
        "type": "null"
       },
       {
        "$ref": "#/$defs/date"
       }
      ]
     },
     "stated_in": {
      "description": "Document whose paragraph states the relationship.",
      "$ref": "#/$defs/document"
     },
     "paragraph": {
      "$ref": "#/$defs/paragraph"
     },
     "description": {
      "type": "string"
     },
     "other_paragraphs": {
      "description": "Optional. Paragraphs of the other document this relationship bears on (e.g. the replaced AD's applicability), cited only for a relationship whose other document precedes this one (supersedes).",
      "type": "array",
      "items": {
       "$ref": "#/$defs/paragraph"
      }
     }
    }
   }
  },
  "dependencies": {
   "description": "Material the screen needs but does not have: service information incorporated by reference, or a table printed only as an image. Parts, actions, and limits point at these by id; an engine that reaches one goes to review naming its title.",
   "type": "array",
   "items": {
    "type": "object",
    "additionalProperties": false,
    "required": [
     "id",
     "title",
     "kind",
     "holds",
     "paragraph"
    ],
    "properties": {
     "id": {
      "$ref": "#/$defs/id"
     },
     "title": {
      "description": "What a person must obtain: the document, its revision, and the table or figure, as the directive names them.",
      "type": "string",
      "minLength": 1
     },
     "kind": {
      "enum": [
       "incorporated_by_reference",
       "image_only_figure"
      ]
     },
     "holds": {
      "enum": [
       "serial_numbers",
       "engine_serial_numbers",
       "compliance_times",
       "procedure",
       "other"
      ]
     },
     "paragraph": {
      "$ref": "#/$defs/paragraph"
     },
     "incorporated_in": {
      "description": "Optional. Paragraphs that incorporate the material by reference , cited whenever the dependency is named.",
      "type": "array",
      "items": {
       "$ref": "#/$defs/paragraph"
      }
     }
    }
   }
  },
  "parts": {
   "description": "Part groups the directive names. A group is found on an engine by part number, or by component name (component or an alias) for its position. serials: any (every serial of these P/Ns), listed (only the rows in listed, each P/N and S/N pair printed in the directive), or listed_in_dependency (the serial list is in unavailable material named by dependency).",
   "type": "array",
   "items": {
    "type": "object",
    "additionalProperties": false,
    "required": [
     "id",
     "component",
     "aliases",
     "part_numbers",
     "serials",
     "listed",
     "dependency",
     "paragraph"
    ],
    "properties": {
     "id": {
      "$ref": "#/$defs/id"
     },
     "component": {
      "type": "string",
      "minLength": 1
     },
     "aliases": {
      "description": "Other names the directive or records use for the same position, used to find the position's record.",
      "type": "array",
      "items": {
       "type": "string",
       "minLength": 1
      }
     },
     "part_numbers": {
      "type": "array",
      "items": {
       "type": "string",
       "minLength": 1
      },
      "description": "Part numbers of the group. Empty means any part number at the named position (the directive names the part but prints no P/N)."
     },
     "serials": {
      "enum": [
       "any",
       "listed",
       "listed_in_dependency"
      ]
     },
     "listed": {
      "type": "array",
      "items": {
       "type": "object",
       "additionalProperties": false,
       "required": [
        "part_number",
        "serial_number",
        "cycles_since_new_limit"
       ],
       "properties": {
        "part_number": {
         "type": "string",
         "minLength": 1
        },
        "serial_number": {
         "type": "string",
         "minLength": 1
        },
        "cycles_since_new_limit": {
         "description": "A per-row part cycles-since-new limit printed in the directive, or null.",
         "anyOf": [
          {
           "type": "null"
          },
          {
           "type": "integer",
           "minimum": 0
          }
         ]
        }
       }
      }
     },
     "dependency": {
      "description": "Dependency id when serials is listed_in_dependency, else \"\".",
      "type": "string"
     },
     "paragraph": {
      "$ref": "#/$defs/paragraph"
     }
    }
   }
  },
  "applicability": {
   "type": "object",
   "additionalProperties": false,
   "required": [
    "engine_models",
    "models_paragraph",
    "engine_serials",
    "parts",
    "parts_combine",
    "parts_paragraph"
   ],
   "properties": {
    "engine_models": {
     "type": "array",
     "items": {
      "type": "string",
      "minLength": 1
     }
    },
    "models_paragraph": {
     "$ref": "#/$defs/paragraph"
    },
    "engine_serials": {
     "description": "Engine serial conditions. Each restricts the models it names to engines whose serial is in a range (inclusive; a null bound is open) or in serial_numbers, and not in excluded. Models no entry names are not restricted. Ranges compare a shared letter prefix and the number after it.",
     "type": "array",
     "items": {
      "type": "object",
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "required": [
       "models",
       "ranges",
       "serial_numbers",
       "excluded",
       "paragraph"
      ],
      "properties": {
       "models": {
        "type": "array",
        "minItems": 1,
        "items": {
         "type": "string"
        }
       },
       "ranges": {
        "type": "array",
        "items": {
         "type": "object",
         "additionalProperties": false,
         "required": [
          "first",
          "last"
         ],
         "properties": {
          "first": {
           "anyOf": [
            {
             "type": "null"
            },
            {
             "type": "string",
             "minLength": 1
            }
           ]
          },
          "last": {
           "anyOf": [
            {
             "type": "null"
            },
            {
             "type": "string",
             "minLength": 1
            }
           ]
          }
         }
        }
       },
       "serial_numbers": {
        "type": "array",
        "items": {
         "type": "string",
         "minLength": 1
        }
       },
       "excluded": {
        "type": "array",
        "items": {
         "type": "string",
         "minLength": 1
        }
       },
       "paragraph": {
        "$ref": "#/$defs/paragraph"
       }
      }
     }
    },
    "parts": {
     "description": "Part group ids that applicability requires installed; empty when the directive applies to the models alone.",
     "type": "array",
     "items": {
      "$ref": "#/$defs/id"
     }
    },
    "parts_combine": {
     "description": "any: one group installed is enough (\"or\", \"either\"). all: every group must be installed (\"and\").",
     "enum": [
      "any",
      "all"
     ]
    },
    "parts_paragraph": {
     "$ref": "#/$defs/optional_paragraph"
    },
    "model_paragraphs": {
     "description": "Optional. The sub-paragraph that names each model, where the applicability paragraph is split into sub-paragraphs; cited with the models paragraph.",
     "type": "array",
     "items": {
      "type": "object",
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "required": [
       "models",
       "paragraph"
      ],
      "properties": {
       "models": {
        "type": "array",
        "items": {
         "type": "string"
        }
       },
       "paragraph": {
        "$ref": "#/$defs/paragraph"
       }
      }
     }
    }
   }
  },
  "eligible_parts": {
   "description": "Parts the directive defines as eligible for installation, by group. A recorded P/N listed here clears its group, with this paragraph cited.",
   "type": "array",
   "items": {
    "type": "object",
    "additionalProperties": false,
    "required": [
     "part_group",
     "part_numbers",
     "description",
     "paragraph"
    ],
    "properties": {
     "part_group": {
      "$ref": "#/$defs/id"
     },
     "part_numbers": {
      "type": "array",
      "items": {
       "type": "string",
       "minLength": 1
      }
     },
     "description": {
      "type": "string"
     },
     "paragraph": {
      "$ref": "#/$defs/paragraph"
     }
    }
   }
  },
  "required_actions": {
   "type": "array",
   "items": {
    "$ref": "#/$defs/action"
   }
  },
  "continuing_obligations": {
   "description": "Obligations that bind while the directive applies, even with no action triggered: installation prohibitions, no alternative actions once done.",
   "type": "array",
   "items": {
    "type": "object",
    "additionalProperties": false,
    "required": [
     "paragraph",
     "description"
    ],
    "properties": {
     "paragraph": {
      "$ref": "#/$defs/paragraph"
     },
     "description": {
      "type": "string",
      "minLength": 1
     },
     "part_group": {
      "description": "Optional. For an installation prohibition, the part group it prohibits; a part of the group recorded as installed after the effective date keeps the screen open.",
      "type": "string"
     }
    }
   }
  },
  "credit_for_previous_actions": {
   "type": "array",
   "items": {
    "type": "object",
    "additionalProperties": false,
    "required": [
     "paragraph",
     "actions",
     "description"
    ],
    "properties": {
     "paragraph": {
      "$ref": "#/$defs/paragraph"
     },
     "actions": {
      "description": "Paragraphs of the actions that may be credited.",
      "type": "array",
      "items": {
       "$ref": "#/$defs/paragraph"
      }
     },
     "description": {
      "type": "string"
     }
    }
   }
  },
  "definitions": {
   "type": "array",
   "items": {
    "type": "object",
    "additionalProperties": false,
    "required": [
     "term",
     "paragraph"
    ],
    "properties": {
     "term": {
      "type": "string"
     },
     "paragraph": {
      "$ref": "#/$defs/paragraph"
     }
    }
   }
  },
  "amoc_paragraph": {
   "$ref": "#/$defs/optional_paragraph"
  },
  "ambiguities": {
   "type": "array",
   "items": {
    "type": "object",
    "additionalProperties": false,
    "required": [
     "paragraph",
     "description",
     "readings"
    ],
    "properties": {
     "paragraph": {
      "$ref": "#/$defs/paragraph"
     },
     "description": {
      "type": "string"
     },
     "readings": {
      "type": "array",
      "items": {
       "type": "string"
      }
     }
    }
   }
  },
  "notes": {
   "type": "array",
   "items": {
    "type": "string"
   }
  },
  "preamble_basis": {
   "description": "Optional. Preamble statements the record relies on, cited as that document's preamble. when: always (relied on for every screen of a listed model), terminating_action_passed (when a terminating action's compliance time has passed), event_before_effective_date (when a triggering event before the effective date is set aside).",
   "type": "array",
   "items": {
    "type": "object",
    "additionalProperties": false,
    "required": [
     "document",
     "when",
     "statement"
    ],
    "properties": {
     "document": {
      "$ref": "#/$defs/document"
     },
     "when": {
      "enum": [
       "always",
       "terminating_action_passed",
       "event_before_effective_date"
      ]
     },
     "statement": {
      "type": "string",
      "minLength": 1
     }
    }
   }
  }
 },
 "$defs": {
  "document": {
   "type": "string",
   "pattern": "^[0-9]{4}-[0-9]{5}$"
  },
  "date": {
   "type": "string",
   "pattern": "^[0-9]{4}-[0-9]{2}-[0-9]{2}$"
  },
  "id": {
   "type": "string",
   "pattern": "^[a-z0-9_]+$"
  },
  "paragraph": {
   "type": "string",
   "pattern": "^\\([a-z]+\\)(\\([0-9]+\\))?(\\([ivx]+\\))?$"
  },
  "optional_paragraph": {
   "type": "string",
   "pattern": "^(\\([a-z]+\\)(\\([0-9]+\\))?(\\([ivx]+\\))?)?$"
  },
  "action": {
   "type": "object",
   "additionalProperties": false,
   "required": [
    "paragraph",
    "description",
    "kind",
    "models",
    "target",
    "operator_condition",
    "unrecorded_conditions",
    "dependencies",
    "csn_band_at_effective_date",
    "trigger",
    "limits",
    "combination",
    "terminates"
   ],
   "properties": {
    "paragraph": {
     "$ref": "#/$defs/paragraph"
    },
    "description": {
     "type": "string"
    },
    "kind": {
     "description": "remove: take the target part out of service (an installed target part means the action is open). inspect, check, revise_maintenance_program, install: work the engine record cannot show as done. replace_if_finding: contingent on a finding of another action; reported, never queued on its own. other: anything else (sent to review).",
     "enum": [
      "remove",
      "inspect",
      "check",
      "revise_maintenance_program",
      "install",
      "replace_if_finding",
      "other"
     ]
    },
    "models": {
     "description": "Engine models this action is limited to; empty for every applicable model.",
     "type": "array",
     "items": {
      "type": "string"
     }
    },
    "target": {
     "description": "Part group id the action acts on, or \"\" for the engine or operator as a whole.",
     "type": "string"
    },
    "operator_condition": {
     "description": "air_carrier_operation when the action binds only air carriers (read from operator.air_carrier_operation); \"\" otherwise.",
     "enum": [
      "",
      "air_carrier_operation"
     ]
    },
    "unrecorded_conditions": {
     "description": "Conditions the action states that no engine record field holds (a part's operating history, whether an earlier inspection was done). An engine the action would otherwise reach goes to review naming them.",
     "type": "array",
     "items": {
      "type": "object",
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "required": [
       "description",
       "paragraph"
      ],
      "properties": {
       "description": {
        "type": "string",
        "minLength": 1
       },
       "paragraph": {
        "$ref": "#/$defs/paragraph"
       }
      }
     }
    },
    "dependencies": {
     "description": "Dependency ids that decide whether or when this action applies (a serial or engine group list, a compliance-time table). Not for procedure-only material.",
     "type": "array",
     "items": {
      "$ref": "#/$defs/id"
     }
    },
    "csn_band_at_effective_date": {
     "description": "Limits the action to target parts whose cycles since new on the effective date fall in this inclusive band (a null bound is open); null when the action has no band.",
     "anyOf": [
      {
       "type": "null"
      },
      {
       "type": "object",
       "additionalProperties": false,
       "required": [
        "min",
        "max"
       ],
       "properties": {
        "min": {
         "anyOf": [
          {
           "type": "null"
          },
          {
           "type": "integer",
           "minimum": 0
          }
         ]
        },
        "max": {
         "anyOf": [
          {
           "type": "null"
          },
          {
           "type": "integer",
           "minimum": 0
          }
         ]
        }
       }
      }
     ]
    },
    "trigger": {
     "type": "object",
     "additionalProperties": false,
     "required": [
      "event",
      "recurrence",
      "condition",
      "definition_paragraphs"
     ],
     "properties": {
      "event": {
       "description": "none: compliance time only. engine_shop_visit: a shop visit as the directive defines it (records assert it per AD). maintenance_event: another defined event the record cannot identify (piece-part exposure, module removal or exposure). part_installation: installing the target part. prior_action: counted from accomplishing another action of this AD (repeat inspections, follow-on removals).",
       "enum": [
        "none",
        "engine_shop_visit",
        "maintenance_event",
        "part_installation",
        "prior_action"
       ]
      },
      "recurrence": {
       "description": "next: the first such event after the effective date. each: every such event, indefinitely.",
       "enum": [
        "next",
        "each"
       ]
      },
      "condition": {
       "description": "A qualifier on the event as the directive words it, or the event's own wording for maintenance_event and prior_action; \"\" if none.",
       "type": "string"
      },
      "definition_paragraphs": {
       "description": "Paragraphs defining the event and its qualifier.",
       "type": "array",
       "items": {
        "$ref": "#/$defs/paragraph"
       }
      }
     }
    },
    "limits": {
     "description": "Compliance-time limits. role caps_event: bounds the event (\"at the next shop visit, but not later than ...\"). alternative: a leg combined with the (capped) event by combination. overall_cap: bounds the combined result (\"..., whichever occurs later, not to exceed ...\"). threshold (2.1): for a recurring (each) trigger, the event counts only once the target part reaches value; below it the action is a continuing obligation.",
     "type": "array",
     "items": {
      "type": "object",
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "required": [
